Linear Search ka matlab hai list mein target ko ek-ek element check karke find karna.

Ex:=
numbers = [10, 25, 7, 25, 40]
target = 40

for i in range(len(numbers)):
    if numbers[i] == target:
        print("Found at index:", i)
        break

Example: list mein 25 kitni baar aaya hai?
Revision 4: Count occurrences

numbers = [10, 25, 7, 25, 40, 25]
target = 25
count = 0

for i in range(len(numbers)):
    if numbers[i] == target:
        count += 1

print(count)
count = 0 se shuru karte hain. Jab bhi target milta hai, count += 1 se count ek badh jaata hai.
Time complexity: \(O(n)\), kyunki poori list check hoti hai.



